                            <votes>0</votes>
                                    <watches>2</watches>
                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="15317365" author="irudyak" created="Mon, 6 Jun 2016 22:07:30 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Actually &quot;cassandra-all-3.3.jar&quot; is used only in Unit tests. It&apos;s compiled with Java 8, cause this version of embedded Cassandra requires Java 8. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thus the more generic question is - what should we do with unit tests for ignite-cassandra module? The thing is that such unit tests could only be executed when you are using Java 8 and fail with Java 7.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15318038" author="avinogradov" created="Tue, 7 Jun 2016 07:27:36 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Igor,&lt;br/&gt;
Tests should be executed for any Java &amp;gt;=7.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But command (release)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt; mvn clean &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;package&lt;/span&gt; -DskipTests&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;runs no tests, so, seems, we can change dependency&apos;s scope to test and it will not cause warning. &lt;br/&gt;
Could you please check it?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15319408" author="irudyak" created="Tue, 7 Jun 2016 20:59:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Ok, fix is available in &quot;ignite-3238&quot; branch: &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/irudyak/ignite/tree/ignite-3238&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/irudyak/ignite/tree/ignite-3238&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is already updated and merged with the latest changes from upstream repository.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15320144" author="avinogradov" created="Wed, 8 Jun 2016 06:57:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Igor, I&apos;ve created pull request from you branch to apache ignite master and see a lot of changes, is it ok?&lt;br/&gt;
PR: &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/783/files&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/783/files&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15321599" author="irudyak" created="Wed, 8 Jun 2016 22:47:33 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;That&apos;s ok. This branch also includes bugfixes to AWS bootstrap scripts which were not included into 1.6 release&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15322106" author="avinogradov" created="Thu, 9 Jun 2016 07:50:47 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Igor, &lt;br/&gt;
Issue can&apos;t be resolved until it merged to master branch.&lt;br/&gt;
Merge should contain only changes related to this issue.&lt;br/&gt;
Please prepare pull request to master branch with required changes, then check it brings no warnings at TeamCity.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After that Issue status can be set to &quot;Patch Available&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Then committer will check and merge changes and change status to &quot;Resolved&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And after that committer will check master branch and close issue in case no problems found. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15323612" author="irudyak" created="Thu, 9 Jun 2016 23:46:34 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi Anton,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I recreated &quot;ignite-3238&quot; branch once again. Now it contains only changes specific to this ticket. Can&apos;t create pull request to &quot;master&quot; branch of upstream repository, probably I don&apos;t have rights for this or you should cancel your previous request first.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15323665" author="irudyak" created="Fri, 10 Jun 2016 00:49:34 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;By the way, what build configuration should I run in TeamCity?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15323678" author="irudyak" created="Fri, 10 Jun 2016 01:03:38 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It&apos;s definitely a problem of the previous pull request you created. Util you close it, I can create a new one from the branch having the same name.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15324099" author="avinogradov" created="Fri, 10 Jun 2016 08:56:59 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Igor, Thanks for branch recreation. &lt;br/&gt;
I closed pull request I&apos;ve made before and created new.&lt;br/&gt;
Now I see only changes related to this task.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;TeamCity Task should be checked is specified at Issue description.&lt;br/&gt;
I checked it at your branch: &lt;a href=&quot;http://149.202.210.143:8111/viewLog.html?buildId=261612&amp;amp;tab=buildResultsDiv&amp;amp;buildTypeId=IgniteTests_RatJavadoc&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://149.202.210.143:8111/viewLog.html?buildId=261612&amp;amp;tab=buildResultsDiv&amp;amp;buildTypeId=IgniteTests_RatJavadoc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
And it works instead of original master branch: &lt;a href=&quot;http://149.202.210.143:8111/viewLog.html?buildId=260834&amp;amp;tab=buildResultsDiv&amp;amp;buildTypeId=IgniteTests_RatJavadoc&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://149.202.210.143:8111/viewLog.html?buildId=260834&amp;amp;tab=buildResultsDiv&amp;amp;buildTypeId=IgniteTests_RatJavadoc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Thanks for your contribution, that&apos;s really important fix, I&apos;ll merge your changes.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15324125" author="avinogradov" created="Fri, 10 Jun 2016 09:19:47 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Merged to master.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15324142" author="avinogradov" created="Fri, 10 Jun 2016 09:36:25 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Master fixed.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
